/target

# Committed on purpose: this becomes an application, and an application pins its
# dependency versions for everyone who builds it.
# Cargo.lock

# §6.1 — the machine-local half of the configuration: where things are on *this*
# machine.
awaseru.local.toml

# And the shared half too, for this repository only. §6.1 says the shared file is
# committed — that is true of a *user's project*. The one here is development
# scaffolding that points at software this project may not redistribute, so it
# stays local as well (§11.2). The committed example configuration arrives with
# the homebrew tutorial, pointing at software that may be shipped.
awaseru.toml

# A vendored reference backend (§16.6) is committed deliberately, never by accident.
/vendor/**/target
